What macOS 27's userland needs of xnu-12377: the system calls its libsystem_kernel calls (pipe2, dup3, fchflagsat,
getumask; ENOSYS without SIGSYS for the ones it probes), a vnode table and workqueue limits for a full userland on one
CPU, and a log line for fatal exceptions and missing system calls. Other Darwin userlands (PureDarwin) also call vfork,
which Apple's arm64 configuration leaves out: it is a fork here.

